Course Gap Analysis — Biomedical Data Science for Industry (2026)
Prepared: 25 October 2026
Scope: Review of all 30 module index files, course survey files, books inventory, and web research on 2026 industry skill demands.
Method: Systematic comparison of existing module topics against (1) 2026 industry skills-gap reports, (2) book inventory coverage, (3) emerging technology domains, and (4) operational completeness of planned vs. complete topics.

[!IMPORTANT] This document identifies gaps only — topics, sub-topics, or entirely missing modules that are not adequately covered by any existing module. Each gap is rated by Priority (P0 = critical; P1 = high; P2 = nice-to-have) and mapped to the most appropriate insertion point in the existing structure.

Executive Summary
The course is exceptionally broad and well-structured. The majority of foundational, clinical, and advanced topics are addressed across the 30 modules. However, six structural gaps and ~40 topic-level gaps exist across the following categories:

